Ok @lilitkarapetyan - I just logged in as `game designer` and stepped forward a few turns. This is what I received:
```
{
  "msg": "ok",
  "data": [
    {
      "gameDate": "2022-05-01T00:00:00+00:00",
      "gameTurnTime": {
        "millis": 259200000,
        "unit": "millis"
      },
      "gameTurn": 1,
      "_id": "2022-09-25T19:29:28.917Z"
    },
    {
      "gameDate": "2022-05-04T01:00",
      "gameTurnTime": {
        "millis": 259200000,
        "unit": "millis"
      },
      "gameTurn": 2,
      "_id": "2023-01-27T16:52:38.201Z"
    },
    {
      "gameDate": "2022-05-04T01:00",
      "gameTurnTime": {
        "millis": 259200000,
        "unit": "millis"
      },
      "gameTurn": 2,
      "_id": "2023-01-27T16:52:44.042Z"
    }
  ]
}
```

I see we get two message for each turn (one for when we switch to adjudication, the other when we switch to planning).  I think we should remove the `_id` field, and de-dupe them. That will give us the information we require.

